        <ArticleTitle>Semaglutide in Patients with Heart Failure with Preserved Ejection Fraction and Obesity</ArticleTitle>
        <Abstract>
          <AbstractText Label="BACKGROUND">Obesity-related heart failure with preserved ejection fraction is a phenotype with few therapies.</AbstractText>
          <AbstractText Label="RESULTS">Semaglutide led to larger reductions in symptoms than placebo (P&lt;0.001), with a mean weight loss of 13.3%.</AbstractText>
        </Abstract>
